window.MONSTER_CHUNK_132 = [{"name":"Clockwork Titan","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"construct","init":0,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+10 natural, -1 size","hp":68,"hd":"7d10+30","hdvalue":7,"fort":2,"ref":2,"will":0,"immunities":["construct traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 slams +12 (2d8+6)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","strength":23,"dexterity":11,"wisdom":6,"charisma":6,"baseatk":7,"cmb":14,"cmd":24,"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","squad (2-4)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature appears as a huge, crablike mechanical monstrosity. It has a saucer-shaped main hull with four spindly legs that sprout from its underbelly and allow it to move with surprising speed and agility. Two iron-shod fists are mounted on the front of its hull.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"In battle, a clockwork titan relies on its reach to keep opponents back.\n\nQuite often, the brain gear attempts to deploy its titans behind a line of clockwork warriors, allowing the titans to rain blows upon enemies without fear of any counterattack.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Crimson Basilisk","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"magical beast","init":0,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":10,"ac_mods":"+9 natural","hp":68,"hd":"8d10+24","hdvalue":8,"fort":11,"ref":6,"will":5,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"bite +11 (2d6+4 plus 1d6 acid)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"acidic bite"},{"type":"blood frenzy"},{"type":"wounding gaze"}],"strength":16,"dexterity":10,"constitution":16,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":12,"charisma":10,"baseatk":8,"cmb":11,"cmd":21,"cmd_special":"+12 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":7,"special":"+17 against stone backgrounds"}],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary","pack (2-5)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature looks like a stocky, 8-legged, crimson scaled reptile. A row of bony spines juts from its back and runs the length of its body. Its eyes have a ghostly blue glow.","group":"Basilisk","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Acidic Bite","kind":"Ex","details":"A crimson basilisk's saliva is corrosive. Any melee bite attack deals acid damage."},{"type":"Blood Frenzy","kind":"Ex","details":"A crimson basilisk that detects fresh blood within 30 ft. enters a frenzied state the following round, along with all other crimson basilisks within 30 ft. Frenzied crimson basilisks fight until they or their opponents are dead. A frenzied crimson basilisk gains a +2 bonus on attack rolls and damage rolls and -2 AC for 1 minute. The creature cannot end the frenzy voluntarily. A crimson basilisk can enter a frenzy only once per encounter."},{"type":"Wounding Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"A living creature within 30 ft. that meets the gaze of a crimson basilisk must succeed on a DC 14 Fortitude saving throw or take 1d3 points of Constitution damage as blood weeps from the victim's eyes, ears, nose, and mouth. Creatures without blood (undead, plants, oozes) and other crimson basilisks are immune to the effects of this gaze. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"Crimson basilisks are variants of the common basilisk, and in some cases more dangerous. Adventurers can be relieved that they will not be turned to stone, but such relief is usually short-lived as they soon realize their equipment begins to disintegrate under acidic bites and they begin bleeding uncontrollably when they meet the creature's gaze. Crimson basilisks are subterranean carnivores with a voracious appetite that is only whetted when they get the thing they desire most-blood. While they can survive on a diet of plants, mosses, and meat, they prefer blood above all else, even attacking their own kind when food is scarce. A typical crimson basilisk lair is a stony cavern that reeks of blood and whose walls and ground are typically covered and caked in dried blood. The lair usually contains up to 5 of these creatures with an equal chance of males and females. From 1d4 young are likely to be present as well. Young don't fight or enter combat. A crimson basilisk is about 6 ft. long and weighs over 400 pounds. Its skin is dull crimson though it can easily change its color (as a free action) to match that of its surroundings. Its eight legs are thick and stout and end in sharpened claws. The spines on its back are crimson as well, though they tend to be darker than its overall body (especially in males). Its eyes glow with a ghostly blue light. A crimson basilisk most often attacks from ambush, using its ability to camouflage itself against its surroundings and lying in wait for prey to wander too close. Once prey moves within 30 ft., it attacks, first using its gaze to bleed a foe and then quickly moving in to bite. If it successfully bleeds an opponent, the basilisk enters a frenzied state and attacks until either it or its prey is dead.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Darnoc","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","subtypes":["incorporeal"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["frightful presence (30 ft.)"],"ac":16,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +4 natural | In ghost form AC 14, touch 14, flat-footed 12 (+2 Dex, +2 deflection)","hp":52,"hd":"8d8+16","hdvalue":8,"fort":4,"ref":4,"will":11,"defensive_abilities":["channel resistance +2","ghost form"],"immunities":["undead traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"slam +7 (1d6+1 plus curse of the grave)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"create spawn"},{"type":"symbol of discord"}],"strength":12,"dexterity":14,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":12,"charisma":14,"baseatk":6,"cmb":17,"cmd":30,"feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Persuasive"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":13},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":10},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":14},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12}],"languages":["Common"],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (2-4)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This entity appears as a translucent humanoid whose face is twisted in an evil scowl. Its eyes burn with a hellish red glow.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Create Spawn","kind":"Su","details":"Any humanoid slain by a darnoc becomes a darnoc in 1d4 rounds. Spawn are under the command of the darnoc that created them and remain enslaved until its death. They don't possess any of the abilities they had in life."},{"type":"Curse of the Grave","kind":"Su","details":"Any damage dealt by a darnoc's slam attack doesn't heal naturally and resists all magical healing (potions, cure spells, and so on). Before the damage can be healed, the curse must first be broken with a break enchantment or remove curse spell (requiring a DC 20 caster level check for either spell)."},{"type":"Ghost Form","kind":"Su","details":"As a standard action, a darnoc can become incorporeal for up to 10 minutes each day. While incorporeal, the darnoc has AC 14 (+2 Dex, +2 deflection) and can use its slam attack as an incorporeal touch against corporeal targets dealing 1d6+1 points of negative energy damage as well as curse of the grave."},{"type":"Symbol of Discord","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day as a standard action, a darnoc can scribe a symbol in the air. All creatures with an Intelligence score of 3 or higher within 60 ft. who see the symbol must succeed on a DC 16 Will save or immediately fall into loud bickering and arguing. Meaningful communication is impossible. If the affected creatures have different alignments, there is a 50% chance that they attack each other. Bickering lasts 5d4 rounds. Fighting begins 1d4 rounds into the bickering and lasts 2d4 rounds. Once triggered, the symbol lasts 2 hours. This is a mind-affecting effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"The darnoc is a corrupting evil presence whose very touch sucks the life from an opponent bit by painful bit. The darnoc are said to be the restless spirits of oppressive, cruel, and power hungry individuals cursed forever to a life of monotony and toil, forbidden by the gods to taste the spoils of the afterlife they so desperately craved in life. Often seen in the clothes and guise it wore in life, a darnoc often walks the same halls and repeats the same actions of its insipid existence over and over again. Due to their great greed, a darnoc may be found within its treasury endlessly counting its coins, or within a graveyard noting the headstones of its vanquished foes with cruel mirth. When distracted from its reverie of its remembered past life, the creature flies into an inconsolable rage, often lashing out without warning or provocation at the first individual who attempts to speak to it.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Death Worm","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["earth"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":66,"hd":"7d10+21 (+7)","hdvalue":7,"fort":8,"ref":6,"will":5,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"burrow","speed":10}],"melee":"bite +10 (1d8+6 plus 1d6 acid)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"spit acid"},{"type":"spit lightning"}],"strength":18,"dexterity":13,"constitution":16,"intelligence":3,"wisdom":11,"charisma":5,"baseatk":7,"cmb":27,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +4 vs. grapple, +2 vs. overrun","cmd":40,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +2 vs. overrun","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":7},{"skill":"Stealth","value":3,"special":"+11 in desert environs"}],"environments":["warm deserts"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature is a long, slender, reddish-brown monster. Its skin is mottled yellow across its back, tapering off as the colors near its head.  Its mouth is huge and lined with rock hard teeth that allow it to break rocks and earth as it burrows underground.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Spit Acid","kind":"Ex","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds, a death worm can spit a stream of acid in a 30-foot line; damage 4d6 acid, Reflex DC 16 half. The save DC is Constitution based. Death worms are immune to their own acid and that of other death worms."},{"type":"Spit Lightning","kind":"Ex","details":"Once per minute on a round in which it doesn't spit acid, a death worm can spit a stroke of lightning in a 20-foot line; damage 3d6 electricity, Reflex DC 16 half. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"The death worm is a reclusive, desert-dwelling creature content to spend its life burrowing beneath the ground and sustaining itself on a diet of sand and earth. On occasion, it surfaces to devour more substantial prey (animals such as moose, deer, bison, and humans).\n\nDeath worms lay their eggs far beneath the surface of the earth.\n\nNewborn death worms live on a diet of sand and earth; only when they reach maturity (2-5 years after hatching) do they surface and devour their first living prey.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Demiurge","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","subtypes":["incorporeal"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["unnatural aura (30 ft.)"],"ac":16,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +4 deflection, +0 natural","hp":68,"hd":"8d8+32","hdvalue":8,"fort":6,"ref":6,"will":28,"defensive_abilities":["incorporeal"],"immunities":["undead traits"],"sr":17,"weaknesses":["vulnerability to iron"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":40,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"incorporeal touch +8 (1d4 cold)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"soul touch"},{"type":"transfixing gaze"}],"dexterity":15,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":14,"charisma":18,"baseatk":6,"cmb":43,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. disarm","cmd":81,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":10},{"skill":"Fly","value":16},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":14},{"skill":"Perception","value":14},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":14},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12},{"skill":"Survival","value":9}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This entity appears as a humanoid with sunken nose, hollow eye sockets, and sickly pale white, semi-transparent flesh. Its hair is unkempt and dirty, and its clothes are nothing more than rags that hang loosely from its translucent form.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Soul Touch","kind":"Su","details":"A demiurge can damage a creature's soul by moving through a space occupied by the creature. This is a standard action that doesn't provoke an attack of opportunity. The target can resist the attack by succeeding on a DC 18 Will save. If the save fails, the target dies as the shock of unlife permeates its soul. If the save succeeds, that creature cannot be affected again by the same demiurge's soul touch for one day. This is a death effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Transfixing Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"Any creature within 30 ft. meeting the demiurge's gaze must succeed on a DC 18 Will save or be transfixed for one minute as if affected by a hold person spell (caster level 10th). An affected creature can attempt a new save each round to break the effects."},{"type":"Unnatural Aura","kind":"Su","details":"Animals don't willingly approach the creature unless the animal's master succeeds at a DC 25 Handle Animal, Ride, or wild empathy check.."},{"type":"Vulnerability to Iron","kind":"Ex","details":"A cold iron weapon ignores the demiurge's incorporeal state and deals normal damage."}],"description":"The demiurge is the undead spirit of an evil human returned from the grave with a wrathful vengeance against all living creatures that enter its domain. The demiurge is very territorial, usually haunting an area of up to three square miles from its place of death.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Dire Worg","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Large","type":"magical beast","init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +7 natural, -1 size","hp":68,"hd":"8d10+24","hdvalue":8,"fort":9,"ref":8,"will":9,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"bite +17 (2d6+13 plus trip)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","strength":29,"dexterity":15,"constitution":17,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":14,"charisma":14,"baseatk":8,"cmb":21,"cmd":35,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (bite)"},{"feat":"Run"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":7},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Stealth","value":5},{"skill":"Survival","value":6}],"languages":["Common","Giant"],"environments":["temperate forests","temperate plains"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","pack (6-11)"],"treasure":"1/10 coins; 50% goods; 50% items","description_visual":"A black-furred wolf the size of a horse, this beast has eyes that seem to glow with a sinister intelligence.","group":"Worg","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","description":"These creatures are to worgs what dire wolves are to their more ordinary kin. They still tend to associate with evil creatures but rarely anything as mundane or insignificant as a goblinoid. Occasionally they serve as mounts for ogres or hill giants. Like their lesser kin, dire worgs typically hunt in packs, though they don't limit their fare to herbivores or the sick and infirm.\n\nDire worgs often challenge the most powerful member of an animal pack knowing that if the leader is killed, the rest are usually easy pickings. They have also been known to seek out isolated humanoid settlements and leave them as little more than smashed buildings and a few well-chewed and bloody bones.\n\nA dire worg has black fur, sometimes with reddish highlights, giving it an almost demonic appearance, and grows to be 10 ft. long and 7 ft. high at the shoulder. It weighs 1,200 pounds.\n\nDire worgs typically attack in packs holding particularly powerful prey at bay until their giant allies or additional worgs arrive. A mated pair of dire worgs often has a pack of normal worgs serving them as bush beaters to chase prey into the dire worgs' clutches. Like their lesser cousins, they prefer to harry and exhaust tougher prey before moving in with flanking and trip attacks.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Dragonnel","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","init":0,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+10 natural, -2 size","hp":76,"hd":"8d10+32","hdvalue":8,"fort":10,"ref":6,"will":6,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +12 (2d6+6), 2 claws +12 (1d8+6)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","strength":22,"dexterity":11,"constitution":18,"intelligence":4,"wisdom":11,"charisma":8,"baseatk":8,"cmb":33,"cmd":42,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Fly)"},{"feat":"Snatch"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":6}],"languages":["Common (cannot speak)"],"environments":["temperate hills"],"organizations":["solitary","pack (2-4)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature looks like a great dragon, at least 20 ft. long with a serpentine body, long slender wings and a pointed snout or beak that resembles that of a pteranodon. Its body is colored reddish-violet with lighter shades on its underbelly. A ridge of maroon-colored spines runs the length of its body down the center of its back. A mane of frills, white in color, rings its head.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"Dragonnels are believed to be either related to dragons or an abomination of dragon and pteranodon, as they share the physical characteristics of both those monsters. Dragonnels are semi-intelligent and use this ability to their advantage when hunting or stalking prey. Dragonnels are fierce hunters, though some have been trained by evil humanoids as mounts and guardians. A typical dragonnel is about 25 ft. long. A dragonnel prefers to attack from the air, flying above its prey and then plunging to strike with its claws and bite. A solitary dragonnel is usually either hunting or returning to its lair from hunting, while more than one dragonnel usually indicates a mated pair or family. In such a case, all dragonnels attack in concert with one another and usually fight to the death. Training a Dragonnel A dragonnel requires training before it can bear a rider in combat. To be trained, a dragonnel must have a friendly attitude toward the trainer (this can be achieved through a successful Diplomacy check). Training a friendly dragonnel requires six weeks of work and a DC 25 Handle Animal check. Riding a dragonnel requires an exotic saddle. A dragonnel can fight while carrying a rider, but the rider cannot also attack unless he or she succeeds on a Ride check. Dragonnel eggs are worth 4,500 gp apiece on the open market, while young are worth 9,000 gp each. Professional trainers charge 1,500 gp to rear or train a dragonnel. Carrying Capacity: A light load for a dragonnel is up to 1,038 pounds; a medium load, 1,039-2,076 pounds, and a heavy load, 2,077-3,120 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Dragonnel originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Ebon Ooze","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"ooze","init":2,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":6,"ac_touch":6,"ac_flat_footed":6,"ac_mods":"-2 Dex, -2 size","hp":100,"hd":"8d8+56 (+8)","hdvalue":8,"fort":9,"ref":2,"will":4,"defensive_abilities":["negative energy affinity"],"immunities":["acid","disease","ooze traits","sonic"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"swim","speed":20}],"melee":"slam +12 (3d6+10 plus 2d6 acid plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"disease","details":"slimy doom, DC 21"}],"strength":24,"dexterity":7,"constitution":24,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":14,"charisma":3,"baseatk":6,"cmb":15,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":23,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Stealth)"},{"feat":"Toughness","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (slam)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Stealth","value":1}],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This is a jet-black, loathsome mass in a roughly spherical shape that slithers forward with a wet slurping sound.","group":"Ooze","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Negative Energy Affinity","kind":"Ex","details":"An ebon ooze is healed by negative energy attacks, and harmed by positive energy, as if it were undead."},{"type":"Slimy Doom","kind":"Ex","details":"Slam-injury; save DC 21 Fort; onset 1 day; frequency 1 day; effect 1d4 Con damage; cure 2 consecutive saves."}],"description":"The ebon ooze is a cousin of the black pudding. It has an affinity for negative energy, and tends to dwell in locations near undead and evil priests. Unlike most oozes, an ebon ooze is intelligent, and takes great pleasure in stalking and devouring living creatures. Although it isn't harmed by sunlight, the ebon ooze finds it painful, and usually takes shelter in a dark, shady location if outdoors during the day.\n\nEbon oozes are ambush predators, using terrain to their advantage to conceal itself until prey draws near. If it feels it clearly outmatches its prey, an ebon ooze may choose to forego grabbing and killing it outright, instead stalking and toying with it. However, when facing a clearly superior opponent, the ebon ooze isn't afraid to retreat, and generally tries to have some means of escape should a fight go against it, such as a deep, narrow crevice or the bottom of a deep pool.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Originally appearing in Rappan Athuk Reloaded (© Necromancer Games, 2006)"},{"name":"Ebony Horse","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["extraplanar","native"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":15,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +6 natural, -1 size","hp":84,"hd":"8d10+40","hdvalue":8,"fort":7,"ref":10,"will":9,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":90,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"2 hooves +7 (1d6+2), bite +12 (1d8+5)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":8,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":13,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"plane shift","details":"self plus five others to elemental planes, Astral Plane, or Material Plane only"}]}],"strength":20,"dexterity":18,"constitution":21,"intelligence":13,"wisdom":17,"charisma":11,"baseatk":8,"cmb":14,"cmd":28,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Run"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":17},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":11},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":12},{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11},{"skill":"Survival","value":14}],"languages":["Common","any two elemental languages (Aquan, Auran, Ignan, Terran)","any one planar language (Abyssal, Celestial, Infernal)"],"sq":[{"type":"elemental endurance"}],"environments":["temperate plains","warm plains"],"organizations":["solitary","herd (2-4)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This large horse has black skin, a black mane, and inky-black hooves.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Elemental Endurance","kind":"Ex","details":"An ebony horse can remain on the Planes of Air, Earth, Fire, or Water for up to 24 hours at a time. An ebony horse can extend this protection to its rider and up to four of the rider's allies in a 30 foot radius around itself. If the ebony and horse and any protected allies move more than 30 ft. apart, the protection ends for that individual and cannot be regained for 24 hours. If the ebony horse is killed, this protection ends immediately. Failure to return to the Material Plane before that time expires causes an ebony horse to take 1 point of damage per additional hour spent on the elemental plane, until it dies or returns to the Material Plane. Other creatures protected by elemental endurance suffer damage normally from the elemental plane when that time expires."}],"description":"Ebony horses are massive stallions prized for their loyalty, running speed, their ability to fly, and their ability to enter the various elemental planes unharmed. These creatures are often used by genies, demons, devils, and others due to their innate ability to withstand the various planar atmospheres and survive unharmed while simultaneously extending this protection to others.\n\nEbony horses are generally solitary creatures but on very rare occasions a small herd of these creatures may be encountered. When not traveling the many planes of existence, ebony horses spend their time roaming vast grasslands on the Material Plane. They don't associate with normal horses or other steeds, preferring to keep company with their own.\n\nEbony horses kick with their front hooves and lash out with a nasty bite when forced into combat. They are strong-willed and brave creatures, rarely backing down when confronted. They are, however, smart enough to know when the battle is lost and take to the air in such times. An ebony horse is fiercely loyal creature to its rider and, if on a hostile plane and protecting a rider with its elemental endurance ability, it will not flee and end this protection, even fighting to its death if necessary. Ebony horses have no known enemies, but tend to show aggression around nightmares. While no known enmity exists between the two, combat is as likely to occur as is no confrontation at all.\n\nLarger ebony horses (10 HD, Huge size) are known to exist and are used extensively by the seraphs (see the Genie, Seraph entry in this book) in their ongoing wars with the efreet.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Eye Of The Deep","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"aberration","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"all-around vision"},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":15,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":15,"ac_mods":"+5 natural","hp":75,"hd":"10d8+20","hdvalue":10,"fort":5,"ref":3,"will":10,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":5},{"type":"swim","speed":20}],"melee":"2 pincers +7 (1d8 plus grab), bite +7 (1d6)","ranged":"eye ray +7 (spell-like ability)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"1d8"},{"type":"eye rays","details":"DC 17"},{"type":"stun cone","details":"30 ft. cone, DC 17, stunned 2d4 rounds"}],"strength":10,"dexterity":10,"constitution":14,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":13,"charisma":13,"baseatk":7,"cmb":7,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":17,"feats":[{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (pincers)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":14},{"skill":"Perception","value":18},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13},{"skill":"Survival","value":14},{"skill":"Swim","value":21}],"languages":["Aklo","Aquan","Common"],"environments":["any aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","cluster (3-6)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature is a 5-foot wide orb dominated by a central eye and large serrated mouth. Hundreds of small seaweed-like bristles hang from the bottom of its body. Two large crab-like pincers protrude from its body, and two long, thin eyestalks sprout from the top of its orb.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"All-Around Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"An eye of the deep's stalked eyes allow it to see in all directions at once. It cannot be flanked."},{"type":"Eye Rays","kind":"Su","details":"Each of the creature's eyes stalks can produce a magical ray once per round as a free action. The creature can aim both of its eye rays in any direction. Each of its eye rays resembles a spell cast by a 12th-level caster and follows the rules for a ray (see Aiming a Spell). Each eye ray has a range of 150 ft. and a save DC of 17. The save DC is Constitution-based. Hold Person Left eye-A target struck by this ray must succeed on a Will save or be affected as though by the spell. An eye of the deep will use this ray early in a fight so as to disable its opponents. Hold Monster Right eye-A target struck by this ray must succeed on a Will save or be affected as though by the spell. This is used in the same manner as the hold person ray. Minor Image By combining the rays of both eyes, the eye of the deep can replicate the minor image spell. It doesn't have to succeed on an attack roll to use this ray. The illusion is generated at any point within range and in the eye of the deep's line of sight."},{"type":"Stun Cone","kind":"Su","details":"An eye of the deep's central eye can, once per round, produce a cone extending straight ahead from its front to a range of 30 ft. Creatures in the area must succeed on a DC 17 Fortitude save or be stunned for 2d4 rounds. The save DC is Constitution-based. Feats An eye of the deep's Flyby Attack feat allows it to take a move action and another standard action at any point during the move while swimming. It cannot take a second move action during a round in which it makes a flyby attack."}],"description":"Eyes of the deep are found only in the deepest parts of the ocean, though on occasion one moves too close to the shoreline and ends up beaching on the sands. An eye of the deep stranded in this manner dies in 2d4 minutes unless placed back into the water.\n\nAn eye of the deep floats slowly through the oceans searching for its prey. It attacks using its eye rays; then it grasps an opponent with its pincers and subjects the victim to its bite attack. An eye of the deep's pincers are considered to be primary attacks.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Eye of the Deep originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1977) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Fachan","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Large","type":"humanoid","subtypes":["giant"],"init":-1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +10 natural, -1 size","hp":73,"hd":"7d8+35 (+7)","hdvalue":7,"fort":10,"ref":1,"will":4,"save_mods":"+4 vs. fear effects","dr":"5/-","speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"greatclub +12 (2d8+10) or slam +11 (2d6+10)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"horrific visage"},{"type":"powerful grip"}],"strength":25,"dexterity":9,"constitution":20,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":10,"charisma":12,"baseatk":5,"cmb":13,"cmd":22,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Toughness","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (greatclub)","type":"bonus"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Intimidate","value":11}],"languages":["Giant"],"sq":[{"type":"one-legged stance"}],"environments":["any land"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (2-5)","tribe (10-30)"],"treasure":"standard (greatclub)","description_visual":"This hideous creature is a bizarre giant that has a single leg, one arm that sprouts from the middle of its chest, and one eye in the middle of its forehead.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Horrific Visage","kind":"Ex","details":"Any creature within 30 ft. viewing a fachan must succeed on a DC 16 Will save or be shaken for 1d4+2 rounds. A creature that makes its save is immune to the horrific visage of that fachan for one day. The save DC is Charisma-based and includes a +2 racial bonus."},{"type":"One-Legged Stance","kind":"Ex","details":"Fachans are surprisingly nimble while hopping on their single leg. This unusual mode of movement allows the fachans to ignore the effects of difficult terrain on movement and makes it impossible to trip."},{"type":"Powerful Grip","kind":"Ex","details":"A fachan can wield a two-handed weapon in its single hand, gaining all the usual benefits for wielding a two-handed weapon."}],"description":"Fachans are foul-tempered and foul-smelling beasts with a taste for human flesh. Despite having only one leg and arm, they are extremely agile. Having only one eye doesn't hamper their vision any more than one leg hampers their mobility. Some sages believe fachans are an offshoot of one of the giant races while others believe fachans are the deformed offspring of a failed hill giant and ogre or cyclops mating. These creatures are shunned by other giant races, except hill giants with whom they have a distant but tolerable relationship. They rarely associate with other races for any reason.\n\nFachans take up residence wherever they can find a warm, dry spot. They are not against building huts and hovels when they must, but they prefer the convenience of driving out the residents of an existing structure and claiming it as their own. They are most often encountered in wastelands and swamps. Fachan villages can consist of up to 30 individuals plus 30% noncombatant young. Fachan leaders are always fighters or barbarians.\n\nFachans stand 12 ft. tall and weigh 1,000 pounds. Their hair is unkempt and matted. Skin tone is usually bronze or brown, and their hair is dark.\n\nA fachan makes for an odd opponent at best. It most often attempts a bull rush against its largest foe in the first round of combat, and tries to avoid spellcasters. After this, it moves in with its melee attacks.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Fanged Sea Serpent","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":24,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +14 natural, -1 size","hp":76,"hd":"8d12+24","hdvalue":8,"fort":9,"ref":7,"will":6,"immunities":["paralysis and sleep","dragon traits"],"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +12 (1d8+6 plus poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"1d8+6"},{"type":"poison"}],"strength":18,"dexterity":13,"constitution":16,"intelligence":5,"wisdom":11,"charisma":6,"baseatk":8,"cmb":13,"cmd":24,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Swim-By Attack","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":9},{"skill":"Stealth","value":6},{"skill":"Survival","value":9},{"skill":"Swim","value":21}],"environments":["any aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","swarm (3-20)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This serpent is 12 to 15 ft. long and 5 ft. thick. Its body scales are thickened and hardened, which slows it somewhat in water but provides good protection. The serpent's most outstanding features, however, are the rows of long, sharp teeth that fill its mouth. It has large, lidless red eyes with white pupils.","group":"Sea Serpent","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite-injury; save Fort DC 17; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d4 Con; cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"The fanged sea serpent is a vicious predator of the seas feared for its tendency to travel in packs and swarm over creatures much larger than itself. Fanged sea serpents are nomadic, traveling with ocean currents.\n\nThey prefer to hunt in groups, which they can surround and attack from all sides. Fanged sea serpents have been known to attack their own kind, but only when starving.\n\nFanged sea serpents on their own usually live on large fish, and avoids confronting intelligent opposition unless they believe their victims to be helpless. However, when they are in groups, they become much more aggressive, and attack creatures much larger than themselves. They prefer to use swarm tactics, surrounding their target and attacking simultaneously from all directions; in the water, where they can also attack from above and below, few marine creatures can stand up to a prolonged assault.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Feral Vampire Spawn","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","subtypes":["augmented human"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +6 natural","hp":68,"hd":"8d8+24 (+8)","hdvalue":8,"hp_mods":["fast healing 2"],"fort":7,"ref":6,"will":4,"defensive_abilities":["channel resistance +4"],"dr":"5/silver","immunities":["undead traits"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"electricity","value":10}],"weaknesses":["vampire weaknesses"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"slam +13 (1d6+10 plus energy drain)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"blood drain"},{"type":"energy drain","details":"1 level, DC 10"}],"strength":25,"dexterity":14,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":6,"charisma":16,"baseatk":6,"cmb":13,"cmd":25,"feats":[{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":15},{"skill":"Perception","value":8},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13}],"languages":["Common (cannot speak)"],"sq":[{"type":"gaseous form"},{"type":"shadowless"},{"type":"spider climb"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","pack (2-5)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This brutish monstrosity appears to have once been a human, though its formerly fine grave clothes are tattered and smeared with the filth of a boneyard. Massive muscles ripple beneath its cold, hard flesh contributing to its hunched posture, and jagged, broken fangs extend from between its bloodless lips.","group":"Vampire Spawn","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Blood Drain","kind":"Su","details":"A feral vampire spawn can suck blood from a grappled opponent; if the feral vampire spawn establishes or maintains a pin, it drains blood, dealing 1d4 points of Constitution damage. The feral vampire spawn heals 5 hit points or gains 5 temporary hit points for 1 hour (up to a maximum number of temporary hit points equal to its full normal hit points) each round it drains blood."},{"type":"Energy Drain","kind":"Su","details":"A creature hit by a feral vampire spawn's slam gains one negative level. This ability only triggers once per round, regardless of the number of attacks the feral vampire spawn makes."},{"type":"Fast Healing","kind":"Su","details":"A feral vampire spawn has fast healing 2. If reduced to 0 hit points in combat, it assumes gaseous form and attempts to escape. It must reach its coffin home within 2 hours or be utterly destroyed. (It can travel up to 9 miles in 2 hours.) Additional damage dealt to a feral vampire spawn forced into gaseous form has no effect. Once at rest, it is helpless. It regains 1 hit point after 1 hour, then is no helpless and resumes healing at the rate of 2 hit points per round."},{"type":"Gaseous Form","kind":"Su","details":"A feral vampire spawn can only assume gaseous form when it has been reduced to 0 hit points in combat. It then assumes gaseous form as the spell (caster level 5th) and returns to its coffin. While gaseous it has a fly speed of 20 ft. with perfect maneuverability."},{"type":"Shadowless","kind":"Ex","details":"A feral vampire spawn casts no shadows and shows no reflection in a mirror."},{"type":"Spider Climb","kind":"Ex","details":"A feral vampire spawn can climb sheer surfaces as though with a spider climb spell."}],"description":"Sometimes when vampires create minions something horrible happens to the creature causing a fate worse than even that of a typical vampire spawn. On these occasions whether by accident or design, upon waking to its new undead existence the newly created spawn finds itself trapped within its coffin or tomb and unable to free itself even in gaseous form. In these instances the spawn rages and struggles to escape as it slowly goes insane, a victim of its all-consuming hunger. When the master vampire finally deigns to release its new spawn or it finally manages to break free - sometimes years after its creation - the spawn is feral and nearly mindless, though with a much greater strength due to its incessant rage. Vampire masters often find such spawn less of a threat and easier to dispose of when their usefulness has ended.\n\nUnlike typical vampire spawn, feral vampire spawn resemble primitive or Neanderthal-like versions of their former selves with heavy frames supporting a massive musculature and a face twisted by rage and hate into an almost animal-like mask. They are usually hunched over from long confinement and weigh up to 200 pounds more than typical for a member of their species of their relative size.\n\nFeral vampire spawn have lost the ability to speak beyond inarticulate roars, though they can understand and obey verbal commands from their master.\n\nFeral vampire spawn attack without thought or tactics using their tremendous brute strength to smash their foes and feed. Though it is presumed that they should still be capable of assuming gaseous form at will or using their domination gaze like standard vampire spawn, feral vampire spawn seem to have forgotten how to use these abilities.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Original author Greg A. Vaughan  Originally appearing in Slumbering Tsar (© Frog God Games/ Greg A. Vaughan, 2012)"},{"name":"Filcher Gremlin","cr":6,"xp":2400,"race":"Gremlin","classes":[{"class":"rogue","level":6}],"alignment":"CE","size":"Small","type":"fey","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":17,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +1 dodge, +2 natural, +1 size","hp":50,"hd":"1d6+6d8+20","hdvalue":7,"fort":4,"ref":10,"will":7,"defensive_abilities":["evasion","trap sense +2","uncanny dodge"],"dr":"5/cold iron","sr":17,"weaknesses":["light blindness"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"short sword +10 (1d4-2), bite +5 (1d4-2) or bite +10 (1d4-2), 2 claws +10 (1d4-2)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"sneak attack","details":"+4d6"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":5,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":7,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"phase door"}]}],"strength":7,"dexterity":21,"constitution":15,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":16,"charisma":13,"baseatk":4,"cmb":1,"cmd":17,"feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Spring Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":15,"special":"+11 jump"},{"skill":"Bluff","value":11},{"skill":"Climb","value":8},{"skill":"Craft (traps)","value":13},{"skill":"Disable Device","value":15},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":15},{"skill":"Perception","value":15},{"skill":"Sleight of Hand","value":15},{"skill":"Stealth","value":19}],"languages":["Common","Goblin","Sylvan"],"sq":[{"type":"rogue talents","details":"fast stealth, ledge walker, quick disable"},{"type":"trapfinding"}],"environments":["any land"],"organizations":["gang (2-5)","pack (6-9)","mob (10-20)"],"treasure":"incidental","description_visual":"This creature resembles a goblin with long floppy ears, a pinched wrinkled face, nasty claws, a mouth full of sharp teeth and a wicked glint to its eyes.","group":"Gremlin","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Knot Expert","kind":"Ex","details":"A gremlin treats its total Hit Dice as its base attack bonus when calculating its CMB to determine the Escape Artist check DC of any restraints it ties using ropes."},{"type":"Phase Door","kind":"Sp","details":"A gremlin can take only other gremlins through the passage and it cannot set triggering conditions to allow others to use the passage."}],"description":"Gremlin filchers are a force to be reckoned with (when it comes to securing your valuables or hiring one to secure someone else's valuables). Their small size and high Stealth bonus allows them to easily slip unnoticed into most places. Their knack with ropes not only aids them in climbing into hard to reach spaces (which could be several given their small size), but also allows them to bind any person(s) who would stop them from their task at hand.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"short sword"},{"name":"Frog Stone Idol","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"construct","init":0,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+11 natural, -1 size","hp":79,"hd":"9d10+30","hdvalue":9,"fort":3,"ref":3,"will":3,"defensive_abilities":["rejuvenation"],"dr":"10/adamantine","immunities":["construct traits (+30 hp)","magic"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"bite +13 (2d6+7)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"crush","details":"4d6+7; DC 16 Ref half"}],"strength":21,"dexterity":10,"wisdom":11,"charisma":1,"baseatk":9,"cmb":15,"cmd":25,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":0,"special":"+8 jumping"}],"sq":[{"type":"powerful leaper"},{"type":"site bound"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","pair"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This giant frog statue has intricate markings and symbols carved into its stony construction.","group":"Stone Idol","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Crush","kind":"Ex","details":"A frog stone idol can land on foes as a standard action, using its whole body to crush them. Crush attacks are effective only against opponents one or more size categories smaller than the frog stone idol. A crush attack affects as many creatures as fit in the stone idol's space. Creatures in the affected area must succeed on a DC 16 Reflex save or be pinned, automatically taking bludgeoning damage during the next round unless the stone idol moves off them. If the stone idol chooses to maintain the pin, it must succeed at a combat maneuver check as normal. Pinned foes take damage from the crush each round if they don't escape. The save DC is Constitution-based and includes a +2 racial bonus."},{"type":"Powerful Leaper","kind":"Ex","details":"A frog stone idol uses its Strength to modify Acrobatics checks made to jump, and it has a +8 racial bonus on Acrobatics checks made to jump."},{"type":"Immunity to Magic","kind":"Ex","details":"A stone idol is immune to any spell or spell-like ability that allows spell resistance. In addition, certain spells and effects function differently against the creature, as noted below. A transmute rock to mud spell slows a stone idol (as the slow spell) for 2d6 rounds, with no saving throw, while transmute mud to rock heals all of its lost hit points. A stone to flesh spell doesn't actually change the stone idol's structure but negates its damage reduction and immunity to magic for 1 full round. A disintegrate spell deals +50% damage to a stone idol. A chaos hammer, holy smite, order's wrath, or unholy blight spell deals 1d4 points of damage per two caster levels to a stone idol if the creator's alignment matches one of the aforementioned spells."},{"type":"Rejuvenation","kind":"Su","details":"Unless a stone idol's main body is shattered into small fragments and scattered to the winds, the creature reforms itself at full strength in 1d4+2 days."},{"type":"Site Bound","kind":"Ex","details":"A stone idol cannot travel more than 200 ft. from a central point designated by its creator. Once this point is selected, it can never be changed. A stone idol taken outside the area ceases functioning until it is brought back into the area."}],"description":"A stone idol frog is about 10 ft. long and weighs 10,000 pounds. It leaps at its foes attempting to crush as many as it can before resorting to its powerful bite attack.\n\nVariant Frog Stone Idol\n\nThe stone idol frog detailed above isn't the only known to exist. One such variant is detailed below.\n\nTsathogga Frog Stone Idol: This creature is identical to the standard stone idol frog. It also gains the following special attack.\n\nVile Croak (Su) Once every 1d4 rounds as a standard action, a Tsathogga idol can unleash a croak that affects all that hear it within 60 ft. Affected creatures take 5d6 points of negative energy damage. A DC 16 Will save reduces the damage by half. The save DC is Constitution-based and includes a +2 racial bonus.\n\nConstruction\n\nA stone idol frog is chiseled from a block of smooth stone that weighs at least 3,000 pounds. It must be of exceptional quality and have a value of not less than 5,000 gp.\n\nFROG STONE IDOL\n\nCL 10th; Price 69,000 gp\n\nRequirements Craft Construct, animate objects, geas/quest, wall of stone, creator must be caster level 10th; Skill Craft (sculpting) or Craft (stonemasonry) DC 16; Cost 37,000 gp.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Gallu-Demon","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+11 natural, -1 size","hp":66,"hd":"7d10+28","hdvalue":7,"fort":9,"ref":7,"will":4,"dr":"10/cold iron","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":17,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 claws +12 (1d6+6 plus grab), bite +12 (1d8+6)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","strength":22,"dexterity":11,"constitution":18,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":14,"charisma":16,"baseatk":7,"cmb":14,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":24,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":13},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":13},{"skill":"Disguise","value":13},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":13},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":12},{"skill":"Stealth","value":6}],"languages":["Abyssal","Common"],"sq":[{"type":"alter shape"},{"type":"dimension door"},{"type":"plane shift"}],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","squad (4-12)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature looks like a 9-foot tall faceless black-skinned humanoid with long wicked talons. Its otherwise featureless face has a mouth filled with rows of sharpened teeth. It wears no clothing or armor of any kind.","group":"Demon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Alter Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A gallu-demon can assume any humanoid form, or revert to its own form, as a standard action. This ability is similar to the alter self spell (CL18th), but the gallu-demon can remain in the new form indefinitely."},{"type":"Dimension Door","kind":"Su","details":"At the gallu-demon's option, it can use dimension door to transport a grappled victim (who gets no saving throw) within the same plane, instead of its plane shift ability. It is otherwise similar to the spell of the same name."},{"type":"Plane Shift","kind":"Su","details":"A gallu-demon can enter any of the elemental planes, the Astral Plane, or the Abyss. This ability transports the gallu-demon and one grappled victim (who gets no save to avoid the shift). It is otherwise similar to the spell of the same name."}],"description":"Gallu-demons are shape-shifting demons of the underworld. They are often employed as soldiers and spies by various demon lords and balors in their abyssal armies. Gallu-demons are quick to anger and hard to control, so companies of these demonic beings are loosely organized at best. Where the gallu-demon excels however, is entering the material planes, disguising itself as a normal humanoid, and abducting a mortal it has befriended, quickly whisking it back to its abyssal lair where it turns said mortal over to its master. Gallu-demons have been known to spend months at a time on the Material Plane just to befriend and eventually abduct a chosen target. Abducted targets are sometimes devoured by a gallu-demon before it has completed its task, but more often than not, an abducted victim is given to the gallu-demon's master who enslaves the victim (or sometimes devours it himself). A gallu-demon stands 9 ft. tall and weighs about 800 pounds. Its flesh is glossy black and other than a large mouth lined with teeth, it has no facial features, though it does seem to be able to see, hear, and smell normally. Gallu-demons attempt to snatch opponents and transport them to the nether spheres of the underworld, where other demons and undead lie waiting in ambush, eager to consume such hapless victims. The galludemon often uses its shape-altering power to approach unsuspecting victims, or to perform special missions such as escorting mortals out of the underworld to claim another in their stead. It must reveal its true form to employ its improved grab ability.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Ghoul Dire Wolf","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Large","type":"undead","init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":90,"hd":"12d8+36","hdvalue":12,"fort":6,"ref":6,"will":10,"defensive_abilities":["channel resistance +4"],"immunities":["undead traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"bite +17 (2d6+12 plus paralysis and trip)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"paralysis","details":"1d4+2 rounds, DC 18"}],"strength":27,"dexterity":15,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":14,"charisma":14,"baseatk":9,"cmb":18,"cmd":30,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (bite)"},{"feat":"Run"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":9},{"skill":"Survival","value":10,"special":"+14 tracking by scent"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","pack (5-8)","mob (2-4 ghoul dire wolves and 4-8 ghoul wolves)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature resembles a wolf with matted dark fur torn away in places. Its flesh is sickly gray where its fur is torn away. Its eyes are stark white.","group":"Wolf","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"Ghoul wolves are carnivorous undead wolves that delight in hunting living creatures, catching them, and tearing them to shreds. These creatures are most often found haunting desolate moors and marshes. Ghoul wolves hunt in packs, surrounding their prey and circling as they move in for the kill.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Giant Death Watch Beetle","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"vermin","init":0,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+9 natural","hp":67,"hd":"9d8+27","hdvalue":9,"fort":9,"ref":3,"will":3,"immunities":["death effects","mind-affecting effects"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +11 (2d6+7)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"death rattle"}],"strength":21,"dexterity":10,"constitution":16,"wisdom":10,"charisma":9,"baseatk":6,"cmb":11,"cmd":21,"cmd_special":"+8 vs. trip","skills":[{"skill":"Stealth","value":0,"special":"+8 in forests"}],"environments":["temperate forests"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature appears as a giant beetle with a dark green carapace and wing-covers. Its body is covered in leaves and sticks. Its mandibles are silver and its legs are black.","group":"Beetle","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Death Rattle","kind":"Ex","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds as a standard action, a death watch beetle can vibrate its carapace to produce a clicking noise that sets up vibrations in all creatures within 30 ft. Creatures that fail a DC 17 Fortitude save take 3d6 damage. Since the effect stems from the vibrations set up in a victim's body and not from the clicking noise itself, silence offers no protection against this attack. Likewise, a creature that cannot hear can still be affected. A successful save renders the target immune to that death watch beetle's death rattle for 24 hours. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Immunity to Death Effects","kind":"Ex","details":"Death watch beetles are immune to any effect that instantly slays it, such as finger of death, slay living, and so on."}],"description":"The death watch beetle makes its lair in forests and uses a mixture of saliva and earth to stick rubbish (leaves and twigs, for instance) to itself in order to attack by surprise.\n\nThe death watch beetle begins combat using its death rattle ability. Any creatures that survive are bitten by the beetle's mandibles and devoured.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Death Watch Beetle originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Giant Electric Catfish","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"animal","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":2,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":75,"hd":"10d8+30","hdvalue":10,"fort":10,"ref":9,"will":6,"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +11 (1d8+6 plus grab)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"electricity discharge"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"1d8+4 acid damage, AC 14, 7 hp"}],"strength":19,"dexterity":15,"constitution":17,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":12,"charisma":2,"baseatk":7,"cmb":12,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":24,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (electricity discharge)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Swim","value":16}],"environments":["temperate aquatic","warm aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary","school (5-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A wide mouthed goggle-eyed fish with slippery grey skin and a puffy, bloated body.","group":"Catfish","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Electricity Discharge","kind":"Ex","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds, a giant electric catfish can generate a pulse of electricity that deals 2d6 points of electricity damage to everything a 10 ft. radius. Living creatures within the area not only take damage but also are stunned for one round. A successful DC 20 Reflex save reduces the electricity damage by half and negates the stunning effect. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Giant electric catfish make their homes beneath fallen logs and in streambed pits where they face upstream with their mouth open, swallowing everything resembling food that should tumble or float into its toothless maw. They favor dank, dark, slow moving or stagnant water with limited visibility. They are nocturnal hunters and venture out a few hours after sunset to hunt. Giant electric catfish are about eight ft. long but can grow to lengths of 12 ft. or more. Its bloated body is generally gray or grayish-brown in color fading to a dull white or cream color on its underbelly. Its eyes are small and its snout wide and round. Three sets of barbels (or feelers) are located around its mouth. Unlike many fish, a giant electric catfish has no dorsal fin. Giant electric catfish are territorial and defend their realms with great ferocity. Before engaging in combat, when threatened or facing a potential enemy, an electric catfish generates a pulse of crackling electricity in an effort to intimidate or discourage would-be predators. Failing this, the giant electric catfish enters combat and bites its foe. A giant electric catfish produces an electrical charge that tends to stun any creature within ten ft. of it. Stunned prey are bitten and swallowed.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Giant Funnel-Web Spider","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"vermin","init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":16,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +4 natural, -1 size","hp":68,"hd":"8d8+32","hdvalue":8,"fort":10,"ref":5,"will":2,"immunities":["mind-affecting effects"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"burrow","speed":10},{"type":"climb","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +12 (2d6+14 plus grab and poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"web","details":"+8 ranged, DC 22, 8 hp"}],"strength":25,"dexterity":17,"constitution":18,"wisdom":10,"charisma":2,"baseatk":6,"cmb":14,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":27,"cmd_special":"+12 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Lunge","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Virulent Poison","type":"bonus"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":23},{"skill":"Perception","value":4},{"skill":"Stealth","value":3,"special":"+7 in webs"}],"sq":[{"type":"hold breath"}],"organizations":["solitary","burrow (2-5)"],"treasure":"incidental","description_visual":"This gigantic spider is glossy bluish-black and hairless. It rears on its back legs and reveals long fangs dripping with venom.","group":"Spider","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Ambush Strike","kind":"Ex","details":"A giant funnel-web spider is particularly adept at moving quickly when its foes are surprised. During a surprise round, a giant funnel-web spider gains a +4 racial bonus on its attack roll."},{"type":"Hold Breath","kind":"Ex","details":"By trapping air bubbles on tiny hairs around its abdomen, a funnel-web spider can hold its breath for a number of hours equal to its Constitution score before it risks drowning."},{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite-injury; save DC 22 Fort; frequency 1/round for 8 rounds; effect 1d4 Constitution and sickened; cure 3 saves. The save DC is Constitution-based and includes a +4 racial bonus."},{"type":"Powerful Bite","kind":"Ex","details":"A giant funnel-web spider applies twice its Strength modifier to bite damage."},{"type":"Strong Webs","kind":"Ex","details":"A giant funnel-web spider's webs gain a +4 bonus to the DC to break or escape."}],"description":"Giant funnel-web spiders are deadly, nocturnal predators that dine on living creatures. Most of their time is spent inside their tube-like lair where they simply wait for prey to pass by. Once prey is detected, they rush to the attack, quickly poisoning their target, and dragging it back into their lair.\n\nGiant funnel-web lairs are large spiraling tubes with open funnel-like mouths, typically built under large rocks, fallen trees, or straight into the ground. The entirely of the tube is covered with thick spider webs. Trip lines radiate outward from the mouth of the lair, up to 100 ft. away. These trip lines signal to the spider that prey is near.\n\nFemale funnel-web spiders are generally larger than males, with shorter legs and thicker abdomens. Females lay several egg sacs a few times each year which quickly hatch. The young rapidly develop and reach maturity within 2 years generally, and leave the lair to go out on their own. Giant funnel-web spiders can live up to 20 years.\n\nA giant funnel-web spider is highly aggressive. If threatened or provoked, unlike other spiders, it rears on its back legs and displays its fangs. This warning position signifies the spider is about to strike. When a funnel-web attacks, its grabs its prey and repeatedly injects it with its deadly poison.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""}];
